<title>FRANCE: Cargo ship runs aground off Corsica.</title>
<headline>Cargo ship runs aground off Corsica.</headline>
<dateline>AJACCIO, Corsica 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Panamanian-registered cargo ship carrying grain ran aground on a small island off Corsica in the Mediterranean Sea early on Wednesday, police said.</p>
<p>The eight crew members of the ship, the Fenes, were brought to safety by rescue workers after the 86-metre (280-foot) craft ran aground, they said.</p>
<p>A small amount of fuel had spilled into the sea but the accident was not considered to be a serious pollution threat at present, officials said.</p>
<p>The cause of the accident was under investigation, they said.</p>
</text>
